	"printer_notes": "EXPERIMENTAL / UNTESTED ON REAL HARDWARE. Drives BOTH Creator 4 extruders (T0 right, T1 left) -- unlike the proven single-extruder profiles this project is otherwise built around. Reverse-engineered from ONE real FlashPrint 5 dual-extruder export (a mirror-mode print, both heads active every layer) -- see docs/DUAL_EXTRUDER_EXPERIMENTAL.md for the full writeup of what was confirmed vs inferred. Key confirmed findings: (1) extruder_offset is 0,0 for both -- firmware handles the physical X/Y offset between nozzles internally, no manual gcode compensation needed (no G92 X/Y, M206, or M218 appear anywhere in the real sample); (2) each active tool maintains its own independent absolute E position, switched by M108 Tn; (3) ~1.0mm retract happens before each tool switch, matching retract_length_toolchange; (4) end gcode needs M104 S0 for BOTH T0 and T1. LEAST confirmed: change_filament_gcode's {next_extruder} placeholder is standard OrcaSlicer convention but not verified against a real marlin-flavor multi-extruder Creator 4 sample -- check the gcode preview shows real M108 Tn lines (not literal unsubstituted placeholder text) before ever attempting a physical print. DO NOT print with this profile unsupervised -- getting extruder_offset or the toolchange sequence wrong risks a physical head collision, unlike anything in the single-extruder profiles.",
